<title>USA: Sparks pegs 1997 U.S. soy acres at 67.5 mln-trade.</title>
<headline>Sparks pegs 1997 U.S. soy acres at 67.5 mln-trade.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sparks Companies pegged 1997 U.S. soybean acreage at 67.5 million acres and corn at 81.9 million acres, trade sources said.</p>
<p>Those figures compare to USDA's June 1 outlook for 68.8 million acres of soybeans and 81.4 million acres of corn.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the Memphis-based analytical firm was not available for comment.</p>
<p>((Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
